meta {
  name: Parse [Weight Words]
  type: grpc
  seq: 9
}

grpc {
  url: {{server}}
  method: /recordsimilarity.v1.Quantities/Parse
  body: grpc
  protoPath: ../crates/similarity-proto/proto/recordsimilarity/v1/similarity.proto
  auth: none
  methodType: unary
}

body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "texts": [
        "eighth",
        "an eighth",
        "quarter",
        "half ounce",
        "half gram",
        "ounce",
        "zip",
        "1/8 oz",
        "half"
      ]
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  A weight the trade names by a word is read as the weight it is sold as, in grams, when the word is the whole text:
  
  - `eighth`, `an eighth`: 3.5 g
  - `quarter`: 7 g
  - `half ounce`: 14 g
  - `half gram`: 0.5 g
  - `ounce`, `zip`: 28 g
  
  A number and a unit stay exact: `1/8 oz` is 0.125 oz, normalized 3543.690390625 mg, not 3500.
  
  `half` alone is refused, `AMOUNT_PROBLEM_AMBIGUOUS_NAME`: it is half an ounce of flower and half a gram of
  concentrate.
}
